TYPES.md §5.1 (index `xs[i]`: the key type for a keyed list; a key argument of hasKey, get and find), §5.3, §7.2: a literal key is checked against the list's key type, so an integer literal out of a sized key's range is E3201 at check time, never only E4002 at evaluation: `bs[300]`, `bs.get(300)`, `bs.hasKey(k: -1)` on a list keyed by a UInt8; `bs[200]` fits. Each names the `keyed by` field it was checked against (API.md §4.4 F12, ERRORS.md §1.5).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record B {
  b: UInt8
}

local let bs: [B] keyed by b = [{ b: 200 }]

local let over: B = bs[300]

local let got: Bool = bs.get(300) != none or bs.hasKey(k: -1)

local let fits: B = bs[200]
-- findings.txt --
error[E3201]  a/a.canon:9:24
  300 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (b: UInt8)

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:11:30
  300 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (b: UInt8)

error[E3201]  a/a.canon:11:59
  -1 does not fit UInt8
  expected by a/a.canon:4 (b: UInt8)

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
